 "intro": "By the river Bagradas, near Utica in Africa, 49 BC. You are Gaius Scribonius Curio, Caesar’s young friend, sent with two legions to take Africa from the Pompeians. King Juba of Numidia is coming to their aid.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, Curio believed deserters who said Juba was far away and only his general Saburra was near. He marched by night, won a small cavalry success at dawn and pushed on with tired men. Saburra fell back, drawing him on, until Juba’s main army arrived and the Numidian horse surrounded the Romans. Curio refused to flee, saying he could not face Caesar after losing his army, and died fighting. Many survivors drowned trying to reach the ships or were killed by Juba. The other choices are what-ifs.",
